INT. REMOTE ISLAND CLINIC - EXAM ROOM - DUSK

A whitewashed room with a single shuttered window. Salt has crusted the sill. The generator stutters somewhere beneath the floor, and the lights breathe in time with it.

DR. IFEOMA OKONKWO-REYES (40s, tired, hair tied with a bandage strip) bends over the examination bed. On it lies SALVADOR MENDES (60s, fisherman, grey in the face), his shirt cut open, a clumsy tourniquet around one thigh. He grips the rail with a knuckle-white hand. At the foot of the bed, NURSE PAOLO FERRARI (30s) holds a bag of saline above his head with both arms trembling.

At the window, MARISOL MENDES (30s, the patient's daughter) holds the shutters closed as though they might fly open. Beside her, LOLO the interpreter, short for Eleuterio (50s, wide-brimmed hat), turns a phone over in his hands.

A radio on the shelf gives a crackle of static, then a voice.

COAST GUARD (V.O.)
Island Clinic, this is Coast Guard Helo Two. Be advised we are forty minutes out. Over.

OKONKWO-REYES
Forty minutes. He doesn't have forty minutes.

FERRARI
Doctor, the pressure.

She watches the monitor. She doesn't answer him. She checks the tourniquet and tightens it a half-turn. Salvador groans.

OKONKWO-REYES
Mr. Mendes. Salvador. Stay with me.

MARISOL
Papa, listen to the doctor.

SALVADOR
(thick, barely audible)
Mari.

Marisol leaves the window and kneels at the bed. She takes his hand. Lolo says something low in Portuguese, and she nods without looking at him.

OKONKWO-REYES
Paolo, take over compressions if I call it.

FERRARI
Yes, Doctor.

OKONKWO-REYES
Lolo, tell her he needs to stay awake.

LOLO
She hears you.

The radio crackles again.

COAST GUARD (V.O.)
Island Clinic, do you copy? Over.

Okonkwo-Reyes lifts the handset without turning from the bed.

OKONKWO-REYES
Copy, Helo Two. Patient is hypovolemic, femoral bleed controlled for now. I need a hoist, a surgeon, and four units of O-negative. Over.

COAST GUARD (V.O.)
Roger. We will relay. Hold tight, Doctor.

She drops the handset and goes back to the bed. Ferrari has not moved. His arms shake but the bag stays high.

FERRARI
Doctor, I can switch with Lolo.

OKONKWO-REYES
No. You're fine.

FERRARI
I'm not.

OKONKWO-REYES
You are. Hold it.

Marisol presses her father's palm to her cheek. The generator coughs. The lights flicker once, twice, and hold. Outside, far off, the first thud of rotor blades.
